  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Branded-residence development in the Caribbean and Latin America is concentrated among luxury hotel operators. The **most commonly associated brands** are:\n\n### Established regional leaders\n- **The Ritz-Carlton / Ritz-Carlton Reserve**\n- **Four Seasons**\n- **St. Regis**\n- **Rosewood**\n- **W Hotels & Residences**\n\nThese consistently rank among the leading hotel brands in the Americas by completed and pipeline residential projects. Marriott International—through Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, W and other flags—is the region’s largest hotel parent company in this sector. ([pdf.euro.savills.co.uk](https://pdf.euro.savills.co.uk/global-research/branded-residences-americas-23-24.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Other frequently encountered luxury brands\n- **Fairmont** and **Raffles**\n- **One&Only**\n- **Aman**\n- **Mandarin Oriental**\n- **Six Senses**\n- **Banyan Tree**\n- **Auberge Resorts Collection**\n- **Waldorf Astoria** and, to a lesser extent, **Conrad**\n- **Park Hyatt**, **Andaz** and **Thompson Hotels**\n- **Kimpton** and **InterContinental**\n- **SLS** and **Mondrian**\n- **Nobu**\n\nExamples include Fairmont Heritage Place Mayakoba, One&Only Mandarina Private Homes, Rosewood Residences Mayakoba, Six Senses developments in Mexico and Grand Bahama, and Waldorf Astoria residences in Costa Rica, Mexico and Turks & Caicos. ([newsroom.hyatt.com](https://newsroom.hyatt.com/news-releases?item=124592&utm_source=openai))\n\n### Additional Marriott flags appearing in newer projects\n- **Autograph Collection**\n- **The Luxury Collection**\n- **EDITION**\n- **JW Marriott**\n\nMarriott formally supports residential products across a broad range of its luxury and lifestyle brands, although Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis and W remain the most recognizable regional residential flags. ([marriott.com](https://www.marriott.com/luxury/about-us?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Practical development shortlist\nFor a typical luxury resort or second-home project, the initial competitive set would usually be:\n\n1. Four Seasons  \n2. Ritz-Carlton or Ritz-Carlton Reserve  \n3. St. Regis  \n4. Rosewood  \n5. One&Only  \n6. Fairmont  \n7. Aman or Six Senses  \n8. W, SLS or Thompson for a more lifestyle-oriented concept  \n9. Waldorf Astoria or Park Hyatt  \n10. Auberge, Banyan Tree or Kimpton for a smaller, differentiated project  \n\nThe appropriate brand ultimately depends on positioning: **Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis and Rosewood** for traditional luxury; **Aman, One&Only and Six Senses** for ultra-luxury resort and wellness concepts; and **W, SLS, Thompson, Andaz and Kimpton** for lifestyle-oriented developments. Hotel brands still account for roughly four-fifths of the global branded-residence sector. ([knightfrank.com](https://www.knightfrank.com/research/article/2025-09-08-the-global-branded-residence-survey-2025?utm_source=openai))",
